.TH OPTION-SHAPES 1 "2026-10-26" "BetterMan regression fixture"
.SH NAME
option-shapes \- distinguish flags from range values, prose, and operators
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
A real command flag with nested values:
.RS
.TP
.B "(-1, 2)"
A numeric interval, as in ffmpeg.
.TP
\-<The address of a label is taken by means of the "gs" modifier>
Multiword prose, as in GCC.
.TP
.B \-<digit>
A real symbolic flag, as in git-archive.
.TP
.B \-<, \-\-less-than
A real literal punctuation flag, as in msgcat and msgcomm.
.TP
.B \-/
A real punctuation flag, as in git-p4.
.TP
.B \-^
A real punctuation flag, as in gpg.
.TP
.B \-\-(heading|footing)-(left|center|right)
A real grouped flag, as in gsbj.
.TP
.B [\-\-password app-specific-password]
A real bracketed flag, as in notarytool.
.RE
.SH Operators
.TP
.B ++ \-\-
Prefix and postfix increment and decrement, as in bc.
.TP
.B \-a
A real command flag is still an option, even under this heading.
.SH "Pathname Expansion"
.TP
.BR +( pattern-list )
Matches one or more occurrences of the patterns, as in bash.
.TP
.B +O
A real plus-prefixed flag is still an option.
